===Climate===
[[File:Shinjuku at 11-28 a.m. on Saturday 8 February 2014.JPG|250px|thumb|right|Heavy Snowfall in Aoyama on 2014]]
Aoyama has a [[wikipedia:Humid continental climate|Humid continental climate]] bordering with [[wikipedia:Humid subtropical climate|Humid subtropical climate]] ([[wikipedia:Köppen climate classification|Köppen climate classification]]) due its high latitude location. Like most of Southern Nakamizu, it has a warm humid summer and a mild cold winter though its summer temperature much higher due to the [[wikipedia:Urban heat island|Urban heat island]] effect around the city. Snowfall rather moderate to heavy due to the Siberian High effect. Aoyama often hit by heavy [[wikipedia:winter storm|winter storm]], [[2012 Sichika Snowstorm|latest one in 2012]] which bring more than 20 inches of snows toward Aoyama.
===Seismic===
Though its not as seismically active as most of major cities on Nakami, Aoyama vulnerable with the megathust earthquake from the plate boundary in the southeast of city. Last Major earthquakes hit include [[1638 Nogizaka Shirakawa Earthquake|1638]], [[1852 Aoyama Earthquake|1852]], and the latest one in [[2011 Rifu Earthquake and Tsunami|2011]].
